 \paragraph{Models and protocol.}
-The checkpoints are Phi-4-mini-reasoning, Qwen3-4B, Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-14B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-\allowbreak Llama-8B and Granite-3.2-8B \cite{microsoft2025phireasoning,yang2025qwen3,guo2025deepseek,ibmgranite2025}. For each budget $c\in\{0,64,128,\allowbreak 256,512,768\}$ we force exactly $c$ reasoning tokens by suppressing end-of-sequence, then read the action in a separate pass as the most likely option letter; the model's own free-text answer is also recorded. Greedy decoding runs under three option orders per scenario (648 decisions per model and budget); five sampled seeds run at 128, 384 and 768 tokens (seed-to-seed s.d. of $q$ at most 0.017); an unconstrained run lets each model stop within 1{,}024 tokens. Completion at 768 tokens inferred from the unconstrained trace matches the forced trace in 96--99.8\% of cases, consistent with greedy forced traces being prefixes of unconstrained ones. A synthetic independent-private-values version with exact payoffs \cite{krishna2010auction} uses the same protocol.
