 \section{Scope and conclusion}
 \label{sec:proxy}
-eBay itself runs proxy bidding, under which bidding one's value is optimal \cite{roth2002lastminute}; rescored that way, the highest menu bid is always optimal and reasoning toward the stated objective lowers quality for five models. Our scoring rule is the pay-your-bid rule of first-price ad exchanges, but we use no ad-exchange data. The calculator is an oracle readout, and the best-evaluated readout uses the parser, so neither is a tool-calling agent with its own failure rate. Forced budgets stop at 768 and natural ones at 1{,}024 tokens, the projection beyond observed lengths is an extrapolation, and routing results reuse the 216 scenarios across folds.
